{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically","id":63110,"title":"Demon mechanically","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-01T14:08:50-08:00","id":63110,"title":"Demon mechanically","content":"So, I checked out the Kickstarter pdf. Awesome book, but it seems maybe a bit more rules heavy than, say, Vampire or Geist or Hunter (games I have actually run). Now, this is without a particularly detailed read of the rules section. So, how is it rules wise? Pretty quick and easy or a bit crunchy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T14:35:00-08:00","id":63120,"title":"","content":"The actual rules for most of the game aren't any more complex than Vampire or Hunter. Embeds and Exploits with fully defined effects aren't any more complicated mechanically than Disciplines or Endowments.<br /> <br /> There is a bit of book keeping load in that you have to select the traits/powers for your demon form, create at least one cover to start out with, and eventually keep track of multiple covers (which can have different Skills and Merits) beyond your normal WoD traits.<br /> <br /> The most complicated parts (IMO) are the undefined and/or open ended bits. There's at least one Exploit (for example) that specifically says that it basically ALWAYS requires GM adjudication, because it's a reality rewrite based on plays on words. Likewise, Pacts are complex (especially since we have a lot of questions about them still) because they are defined by players in game, and Interlocks and the Cipher are a pretty big GM workload.<br /> <br /> For each player, as GM, you have to select 4 Embeds to serve as their personal key. They don't get to know what they are. Then, you have to create three Interlocks, which are hybrid powers built from the Embeds in their Key. And lastly you have to determine their Cipher, so that when they have discovered and learned all 4 of their Keys you can reward them with the Cipher, which is basically a piece of concrete advice on how to achieve their own personal Hell (Demon's answer to Golconda/Apothesis/Ascension/Promethean rebirth/ETC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T14:37:48-08:00","id":63124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=63120#post63120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For each player, as GM, you have to select 4 Embeds to serve as their personal key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three. The player picks their first, as only makes sense given that it's one of the Embeds you start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T14:56:04-08:00","id":63133,"title":"","content":"I've found that the most, shall we say, labor-intensive part of running Demon isn't at the game table. Instead, working up characters' Ciphers and so forth, and things like that, take up some time. <br /> <br /> During game, I never had to do much in the way of heavy lifting for the rules, since everything does tend to flow rather well once you're used to it. (And that took me a session or two, I'll admit.) However, once you have it, you have it - and most of it is just off of the base rules anyway, so get those down first, and then you'll have a much easier transition layering things on top of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T08:24:23-08:00","id":63438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=63124#post63124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three. The player picks their first, as only makes sense given that it's one of the Embeds you start with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I remembered that one of their starting Embeds was a key, I didn't remember that the player got to decide which one was their first key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T12:57:45-08:00","id":63559,"title":"","content":"While I haven't had a chance to play yet... I imagine that most of the weight coming up during play is going to be Cover. Everything else can either be jotted down on a sheet or easily referenced during play; you don't need to know every embed and exploit, just the ones your characters are using. Making a gadget is a one time thing. <br /> <br /> Ciphers are a pain; I'm hoping Flowers will have an expanded section for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T13:15:03-08:00","id":63567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=63559#post63559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ciphers are a pain; I'm hoping Flowers will have an expanded section for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, Ciphers have been the most fun for me so far, to the degree that I've got a folder full of larval Ciphers to develop NPCs for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T19:59:21-08:00","id":63706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=63559#post63559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ciphers are a pain; I'm hoping Flowers will have an expanded section for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ciphers are tricky for me as well. I imagine I'm overthinking them in some way though, honestly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:00:36-08:00","id":63880,"title":"","content":"Well, I envision Ciphers as the &quot;z-axis&quot; of DtD. Its like creating a unique bloodline or lodge for every single character that comes around. Some people find it easy and enjoy it. Others don't.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:15:37-08:00","id":64053,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of mechanics, how do Demons stack up against vampires power wise? Can a starting demon and a starting vampire keep pace with one another? How about BP/P 3/5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2174-helter-skelter","name":"Helter Skelter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:24:46-08:00","id":64060,"title":"","content":"Probably. There's a greater sense of cohesive growth to Disciplines compared to the divide of Embeds and Exploits clear power, but it should balance out more or less.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, vampires sit between Embeds and Exploits nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T16:25:04-08:00","id":64394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helter Skelter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=64053#post64053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of mechanics, how do Demons stack up against vampires power wise? Can a starting demon and a starting vampire keep pace with one another? How about BP/P 3/5?</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the circumstances? What's the context of the meeting? Why are the two interacting, and how do they know what the other is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:08:35-08:00","id":64424,"title":"","content":"A demon Going Loud is probably going to be more powerful than all but an elder vampire; it make signal angels, but it . Cover gives them insane high defense against younger vampire mental powers - most vampire powers call for contested rolls instead of subtracting anything, while changelings and fellow demons rarely have contested powers.<br /> <br /> So, in a white room brawl, demons come out better due to easy access to higher potency in short bursts.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, fighting off a vampire invariably degrades their Cover nastily - shrugging off dominate and not realizing it was a mental effect (no reason they should realize it!) leads to investigation (arguably a compromise just when a &quot;mere mortal&quot; shrugs off dominate without realizing it!). Going Loud is a risk, as you still aren't more powerful than teams of rank 4 angel hit squads. All of a demon's high level powers and transformations call for Cover Compromises, which is bad for them. &quot;Exposure&quot; is the bane of demons as fire is for vampires.<br /> <br /> As well, the Kiss is not a contested check, and vitae addiction/bonds are harsh mistresses which demons may not be protected against.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, long story short. Demons have some very nice powers they kick off with to beat neonates, but risk getting taken out by angels. At mid-levels, things even out a lot. At high levels, vampires probably have an upper hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-03-2014, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:32:41-08:00","id":65013,"title":"","content":"Just stating the ironical nature of asking about the &quot;Mechanics&quot; of the Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T12:57:27-08:00","id":67352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=64424#post64424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, long story short. Demons have some very nice powers they kick off with to beat neonates, but risk getting taken out by angels. At mid-levels, things even out a lot. At high levels, vampires probably have an upper hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the circumstances? What's the context of the meeting? Why are the two interacting, and how do they know what the other is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly curious about a straight up physical contest between the two. Let's say both meet in the ally and just start beating on one another with their fists. Vampires have quite a bump due to Vigor, not to mention spending Vitae to up their damage even further. I was mostly curious to see if Demons could throw around similarly high die pools for physical attacks without &quot;going loud&quot; just using their &quot;base&quot; abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2174-helter-skelter","name":"Helter Skelter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T13:24:53-08:00","id":67376,"title":"","content":"Depends on their specific abilities, but let me put it like this, a demon that specs for killing will be a terror to fight, probably even for a vampire.<br /> The downside of course is that even if they don't go loud the exploits and embeds they would use would put their cover at risk, if not outright break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T15:23:45-08:00","id":67442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helter Skelter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=67352#post67352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mostly curious about a straight up physical contest between the two. Let's say both meet in the ally and just start beating on one another with their fists. Vampires have quite a bump due to Vigor, not to mention spending Vitae to up their damage even further. I was mostly curious to see if Demons could throw around similarly high die pools for physical attacks without &quot;going loud&quot; just using their &quot;base&quot; abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, vampires also have frenzy, which adds their Blood Potency to their physical attacks. And take bashing from most every kind of damage out there. Lets also throw on the frenzy FS. Lets not forget something like the effects of Predator's Aura, which can inflict penalties in this fight (assuming its successful).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there's a demon. Lets say a Destroyer, since beating people up is their thing. First of all, they get some really nice powers and effects from their Demon Form. Gun/sword/clawed arms, attribute boosts, armor, unusual movement such as flight and teleports, poison tails, acid spit, electricity, fire, shields / illusions, extra limbs, turn into an insect swarm, magnesium flares, reflexive healing. Most embeds and exploits won't work here - as we've established the vamp is using Vigor instead of Majesty or Dominate or similar, I'm going to stick with direct combat application stuff. There's two embeds dealing with healing/damage mitigation, and one embed and one exploit dealing with guns. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of potential power here. Exposure is the demon's bane; so I'm going to assume that the demon won't use fire, and that Cover will be ignored for the moment (both vamps and demons have ways of negating / lessening their bane, so for the sake of simplicity, I'm assuming that's true now. Otherwise, this would be a very quick battle, very likely with the vampire dead, and the demon surrounded by hunter angels.) Both have a wide range of natural abilities. <br /> <br /> I would have to give the starting vampire the advantage in this case, where they both start punching / stabbing each other. The sheer amount of dice they get is staggering. Vampires natural resistance to damage I think is roughly equivalent to all the armor the demon can put on. And that's before we start investing in Resilience for more. <br /> <br /> All in all, this style of fighting just favors vampires over demons - despite being the social game, vampires are very direct creatures, and most of their powers and advantages reflect this. Domination and control is a thing with them; they get up in your face, and beat you down. Demons, on the other hand, are spies - they have a much greater advantage over vampires when it comes to a hide-and-seek battle, or just plain mobility. They have better powers when using guns - combine with a teleport demon form ability? Or wings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T02:06:17-08:00","id":67798,"title":"","content":"If you want to construct a Demon that cannot not be defeated by a Vampire in physical combat, you can do so.<br /> <br /> E.g. if your demonic form includes the process Insect Swarm you can turn into a million tiny insects and cannot be killed by normal physical violence (if you activate only that power from your demonic form, you get a huge bonus on your compromise roll, +1 for each demonic form power not activated, so you don't really endanger your cover, even if you do it before human witnesses). Then, summon an insect swarm with the Swarm exploit and let the vampire take automatic bashing damage each turn equal to your primum (use a willpower point and you don't even roll for compromise). I have used that on my vampire players with a primum 6 demon. Vampires were fear frenzying left and right (I admit Swarm says 'living target' but why would something that lets a human take six bashing damage a turn not harm a vampire's body ? You could also just have the demon throw fire for 6 leathal at them).<br /> <br /> If you really want just physical stats, well, the demonic form can include for example. Swordarm (4L Weapon), superhuman strength (+2), Armored plates (3/2 Armor), huge form (+ 4size = +4 health levels), Wound Healing (heal rightmost health box every turn). You can choose to activate only a bunch of these to get bonuses to compromise as described above. Also, when turning into full demonic form, you heal damage equal to your primum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 02-08-2014, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T07:17:59-08:00","id":67884,"title":"","content":"Sure, you could do insect swarm. But the same can be true of a vampire getting Protean and that ability as well - pretty sure the swarm merit is now only Protean 3, well within starting PC range. Probably the most powerful ability in Vampire, however, is Dominate. The ability to take control of an opponent is nothing to sneer at. But, even then, we were asked to compare Vigor to a demon. So, I aimed to compare physical stat boosting stuff. <br /> <br /> Doing anything else outside this white room scenario leads to far too much complexity. In the end, however, it comes down to one thing: &quot;Is the situation playing towards one or the other's strengths, but not the other's? Y/N&quot; Vampires will tend to win when they can employ their controlling tendencies. Demons when they can employ their stealth and subterfuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:52:18-08:00","id":69272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=67442#post67442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to give the starting vampire the advantage in this case, where they both start punching / stabbing each other. The sheer amount of dice they get is staggering. Vampires natural resistance to damage I think is roughly equivalent to all the armor the demon can put on. And that's before we start investing in Resilience for more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what I was interested in, just seeing the max dice a vampire or demon could put down for a single physical attack. Thanks for the write up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want just physical stats, well, the demonic form can include for example. Swordarm (4L Weapon), superhuman strength (+2), Armored plates (3/2 Armor), huge form (+ 4size = +4 health levels), Wound Healing (heal rightmost health box every turn). You can choose to activate only a bunch of these to get bonuses to compromise as described above. Also, when turning into full demonic form, you heal damage equal to your primum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was looking for, thanks for posting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2174-helter-skelter","name":"Helter Skelter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T21:48:25-08:00","id":69626,"title":"","content":"See, I think 'balance' or inter-splat power comparison is not really all that important, as they are not even designed with (too much) crossover in the developers' minds. Demons are (mostly) designed to deal with GM and angels(and other demons) in many different ways, while vampires got mostly other vampires, mages got the seers/banishers/whatever, werewolves spirits and such.<br /> <br /> Although I really do love Demon the Descent, I do think the game concentrates WAY too much on the 'techgnostic' side / espionage, and downplays the actual 'demonic' imagery way too much. I love VtR and Changeling because they fit the image of the traditional / mass-media-portrayed vampires and changelings pretty well, and I don't love werewolves as much because they are more spirit doctor / Native American medicine men than beastly-horrifying-halfman half wolf.<br /> <br /> Just the matter of preferences, really. However, when I now think of Demon the Descent, the image that comes up is not a demon, but a cyborg spy. Not that it's a bad thing though. but yeah.<br /> <br /> (And I do think powerful demons should be more powerful. I barely played demon at this point, and didn't get to play higher-exp demons yet, but seems like there's less merit to, say, raising primum and the penalties are way too big. I do hope they do add something in the other books that makes higher-level demons more terrifying.) Maybe I could houserule it, maybe I'll love DtF translation guide...<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah... coming to think about it, the DtF advantage of being immune from mind control and soul altering could really fit well with DtD, but well. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T22:13:57-08:00","id":69638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69626#post69626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... coming to think about it, the DtF advantage of being immune from mind control and soul altering could really fit well with DtD, but well.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Demon in their cover is already hilariously resistant to any resisted Supernatural abilities. Considering that their Cover Rating is used in place of Primum for Powerstat resistance when covered, that's going to be a tough roll for all but the most ridiculously potent mind controllers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T00:22:38-08:00","id":69669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69638#post69638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Demon in their cover is already hilariously resistant to any resisted Supernatural abilities. Considering that their Cover Rating is used in place of Primum for Powerstat resistance when covered, that's going to be a tough roll for all but the most ridiculously potent mind controllers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that is nearly impossible to tell if one of the Unchained are giving you the complete truth or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T03:34:23-08:00","id":69733,"title":"","content":"I've been reading through the text, and one thing stands out about Demon more than anything thematically.<br /> <b>I'm not playing a Demon. I am playing a Virtual Adept.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T05:04:29-08:00","id":69765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69638#post69638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Demon in their cover is already hilariously resistant to any resisted Supernatural abilities. Considering that their Cover Rating is used in place of Primum for Powerstat resistance when covered, that's going to be a tough roll for all but the most ridiculously potent mind controllers.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. You're best off, when confronting a demon, to either have buffs in place on yourself, or to have abilities that come at things sideways. Direct mental attacks on demons tend to fail. Actually, I just realized that direct attacks do as well - I forgot about Just Bruised. &quot;Hi, I only take 1 damage from your attack.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:47:21-08:00","id":69907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69626#post69626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I think 'balance' or inter-splat power comparison is not really all that important, as they are not even designed with (too much) crossover in the developers' minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's my understanding that this is the common school of thought, which frankly I can't stand. They're all in the World of Darkness, and other splats can make great antagonists. I know when I run a WoD game the &quot;primary&quot; antagonist is only so interesting in so far as surprising players with abilities. It can be a lot of fun to cross the splats over and get players involved in worlds they don't belong in. In my eyes, if they all live in the same world (which they do) then balance considerations should absolutely be made for when they run into each other (which they should).<br /> <br /> Rant over, just a personal opinion. I hear you but I wish this wasn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2174-helter-skelter","name":"Helter Skelter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T21:20:43-08:00","id":70294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helter Skelter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69907#post69907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's my understanding that this is the common school of thought, which frankly I can't stand. They're all in the World of Darkness, and other splats can make great antagonists. I know when I run a WoD game the &quot;primary&quot; antagonist is only so interesting in so far as surprising players with abilities. It can be a lot of fun to cross the splats over and get players involved in worlds they don't belong in. In my eyes, if they all live in the same world (which they do) then balance considerations should absolutely be made for when they run into each other (which they should).<br /> <br /> Rant over, just a personal opinion. I hear you but I wish this wasn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seriously though, I wholeheartedly agree with you. I really do wish there were inter-splat balance.<br /> <br /> Arguably, more than anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can always houserule, but it's never really the same...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T03:18:58-08:00","id":71138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=63120#post63120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For each player, as GM, you have to select 4 Embeds to serve as their personal key. They don't get to know what they are. Then, you have to create three Interlocks, which are hybrid powers built from the Embeds in their Key. And lastly you have to determine their Cipher, so that when they have discovered and learned all 4 of their Keys you can reward them with the Cipher, which is basically a piece of concrete advice on how to achieve their own personal Hell (Demon's answer to Golconda/Apothesis/Ascension/Promethean rebirth/ETC).</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't players themselves choose those? Not only it would unload Storyteller, but also make more perfect sense with they individuality on character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:29:14-08:00","id":71162,"title":"","content":"Should, yes, that's likely ideal. I know I find it annoying when the ST decides what my character has to buy in terms of powers. Hells, what happens if the ST misreads the character and designs the imbeds with a set of keys that the PC would never choose to take for various reasons? Or the character changes mid-game through development?<br /> <br /> Also, much of the Chronicle line seems to be fond of putting a lot of work on the STs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-13-2014, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T06:26:06-08:00","id":71220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71162#post71162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should, yes, that's likely ideal. I know I find it annoying when the ST decides what my character has to buy in terms of powers. Hells, what happens if the ST misreads the character and designs the imbeds with a set of keys that the PC would never choose to take for various reasons? Or the character changes mid-game through development?<br /> <br /> Also, much of the Chronicle line seems to be fond of putting a lot of work on the STs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The players get to pick the 1st Key Embed, so that has a large influence on the Cipher overall. I'm running a campaign that has been going on since the week the preview pdf came out in the kickstarter and all 4 players have figured out their Ciphers at this point. I was worried that I might not have gotten some of them right, but all of the players loved theirs. I posted them here as examples if anyone needs some ideas. And if the character changes midgame and hasn't finished their Cipher yet, the ST is always free to change the parts of it that they have not figured out yet. <br /> <br /> But you are definitely right, there is a lot of work put on the ST. Although not as much as I think that they put on STs for Mummy. Haven't played or ran that, but reading through it sounds like a ton of work for the STs since the players don't come up with backgrounds, the STs come up with thousands of years of background for the players to find out about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:25:29-08:00","id":71325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hulsmanm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71220#post71220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The players get to pick the 1st Key Embed, so that has a large influence on the Cipher overall. I'm running a campaign that has been going on since the week the preview pdf came out in the kickstarter and all 4 players have figured out their Ciphers at this point. I was worried that I might not have gotten some of them right, but all of the players loved theirs. I posted them here as examples if anyone needs some ideas. And if the character changes midgame and hasn't finished their Cipher yet, the ST is always free to change the parts of it that they have not figured out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah. I just don't like how the rules say the ST has to know the cyphers, or the Promethean milestones, etc. There should be a focus on player-ST cooperation doing it, instead of the ST writing it themselves. <br /> <br /> I guess I like a focus on story telling then mystery solving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:41:53-08:00","id":71420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=69733#post69733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading through the text, and one thing stands out about Demon more than anything thematically.<br /> <b>I'm not playing a Demon. I am playing a Virtual Adept.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you are playing a rogue MUSH admin who has decided to try to fit in with the mobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:55:07-08:00","id":71434,"title":"","content":"MissMaddy, please don't take this the wrong way, but right now I could kiss you. +1 for perfect comedic response.<br /> I really needed that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:15:04-08:00","id":71449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=64424#post64424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, fighting off a vampire invariably degrades their Cover nastily - shrugging off dominate and not realizing it was a mental effect (no reason they should realize it!) leads to investigation (arguably a compromise just when a &quot;mere mortal&quot; shrugs off dominate without realizing it!).</div> </div> </div> </div>A note here - I haven't found Investigation is really that much of an issue for any Demon with a decent cover.<br /> <br /> Let's examine the Mechanics - Wits + Occult is not a super pool for most people, but let's take the hyperbolic example of Dr Strange who has Wits 5 and Occult 5. He's met a Demon who recently fell, but has had a few issues, so the cover of the Demon is 6.<br /> <br /> So, after getting the sense that something is 'not quite right' about the demon, Dr Strange decides to investigate him. In order to earn his first Wits + Occult roll, he has to dedicate an entire DAY to researching this thing - and let's keep in mind, that isn't a day where he's finding lots of little bits of intriguing information that affirm his suspicions. No, it's an entire day where he looks into it, finds that pretty much everything seems normal, and yet for some reason decides to keep sinking his time into this.<br /> <br /> So, after that full 8 hour research session of coming up with NOTHING, he rolls. He does fantastic. He gets 4 succs on 10 dice.<br /> <br /> Despite the fact that he didn't find anything unusual after eight hours of searching, he's now gonna hafta go back into the research mines and put ANOTHER full day into this.<br /> <br /> Finally, after reading and researching things that indicate the Demon is COMPLETELY NORMAL for -16 hours-, Dr Strange makes another roll and matches the demon's cover.<br /> <br /> He finds a mistake and the Demon suffers a compromise.<br /> <br /> Now, that's -kinda- a big deal?... but for 99.99 percent of situations, around hour 3... before the investigator even gets the first ROLL... they're gonna be like, 'fuck this shit, I was wrong'.<br /> <br /> So, investigations are not as dangerous as they might seem.<br /> <br /> Do keep in mind that the previous example used only a Cover 6 demon with the pinnacle of human perfection in investigating covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:35:11-08:00","id":71517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71449#post71449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, investigations are not as dangerous as they might seem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless someone is investigating you for an unrelated reason (unrelated to the character being a Demon that is).<br /> <br /> Maybe you commited a murder and the police is after you, or maybe you have enemies who know about your condition and think it is fun to have you investigated by a private investigator. In such cases a Demon could have a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:16:26-08:00","id":71609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71449#post71449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after getting the sense that something is 'not quite right' about the demon, Dr Strange decides to investigate him. In order to earn his first Wits + Occult roll, he has to dedicate an entire DAY to researching this thing - and let's keep in mind, that isn't a day where he's finding lots of little bits of intriguing information that affirm his suspicions. No, it's an entire day where he looks into it, finds that pretty much everything seems normal, and yet for some reason decides to keep sinking his time into this.<br /> <br /> So, after that full 8 hour research session of coming up with NOTHING, he rolls. He does fantastic. He gets 4 succs on 10 dice.<br /> <br /> Despite the fact that he didn't find anything unusual after eight hours of searching, he's now gonna hafta go back into the research mines and put ANOTHER full day into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first paragraph of the &quot;Investigating a Demon&quot; sidebar would seem to put the lie to &quot;that isn't a day where he's finding lots of little bits of intriguing information&quot; and &quot;coming up with NOTHING,&quot; and &quot;I watched the guy for one day&quot; is on rather the opposite end of the scale from &quot;determined attention&quot; and &quot;persistent investigation.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do keep in mind that the previous example used only a Cover 6 demon with the pinnacle of human perfection in investigating covers. </div> </div> </div>Professional Training (Occultist) is not to be underestimated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:33:40-08:00","id":71622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71449#post71449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A note here - I haven't found Investigation is really that much of an issue for any Demon with a decent cover.<br /> <br /> Do keep in mind that the previous example used only a Cover 6 demon with the pinnacle of human perfection in investigating covers.</div> </div> </div> </div> It takes a while from mundane investigation rolls, perhaps. But I was thinking more along the lines of the demon acting out of character. Demons cannot maintain a perfect Cover all the time - if someone's watching them, or digging into backgrounds, and you can just sit in a single Cover for the length of time? Not a big deal. If they need to switch between several covers? Or go on a job? Make a Pact? Things get trickier. You -have- to act out of character in front of your watchers then, which will provoke Compromise rolls. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:24:02-08:00","id":71658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71517#post71517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless someone is investigating you for an unrelated reason (unrelated to the character being a Demon that is).<br /> <br /> Maybe you commited a murder and the police is after you, or maybe you have enemies who know about your condition and think it is fun to have you investigated by a private investigator. In such cases a Demon could have a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's certainly agreed. SOME sources of sustained investigation exist and those are to be avoided like the plague... being on the Most Wanted List will degrade your cover pretty damn quick... but in a more casual setting, your cover will provide pretty good protection for most situations.<br /> <br /> Ordinary people... like, 2-5 dicers... are gonna hafta sink like an entire week of work into finding just -one- compromise inducing fact, and very few folks are gonna be compelled to go that length without serious motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 02-13-2014, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:34:12-08:00","id":71664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71658#post71658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ordinary people... like, 2-5 dicers... are gonna hafta sink like an entire week of work into finding just -one- compromise inducing fact, and very few folks are gonna be compelled to go that length without serious motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the digital trail of most people are full of compromising weirdness. Just taking one look at most of our browser history is probably enough for polite society to freak out. So even mundane people investigating your cover are not likely to arrive at a supernatural conclusion. Even those that do are probably going to arrive at the wrong supernatural conclusion.<br /> <br /> Being the Truth Police generally wastes everyone's time. We're all full of inconsistencies. Even our own memories are flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 02-13-2014, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T00:42:48-08:00","id":71858,"title":"","content":"I've wondered where the hell you'd actually research a G-M angel like that. Regular spirits or Ghosts I get, but angels? Particularly with how they might be constructed just for that task?<br /> <br /> Hau, I say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T04:39:21-08:00","id":71906,"title":"","content":"There is this quote: &quot;Smart demons maintain libraries and research about the banes of ephemeral entities, focusing on those who match descriptions of angels, because utilizing banes are one of the only ways a demon can get an advantage over her hunter.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it's not *that* helpful. Unless the implication is that by observing similar angels you can deduce their banes even if the individual angel is a one-mission pony that gets recycled in the end... I dunno...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Where does it say that the rolls take 30 min each? I can't seem to find that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","user":"genesis","date":". 02-14-2014, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T05:33:29-08:00","id":71919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63110-demon-mechanically?p=71906#post71906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is this quote: &quot;Smart demons maintain libraries and research about the banes of ephemeral entities, focusing on those who match descriptions of angels, because utilizing banes are one of the only ways a demon can get an advantage over her hunter.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it's not *that* helpful. Unless the implication is that by observing similar angels you can deduce their banes even if the individual angel is a one-mission pony that gets recycled in the end... I dunno...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Where does it say that the rolls take 30 min each? I can't seem to find that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most angels tend to be reused; its hard to actually make an angel whole cloth. Its part of why demons are hunted - to recycle them back into angels. So, there's a chance someone's run into this particular angel before, and observed its bane/ban before. Ergo, the research. <br /> <br /> Making a new angel like Y2K is a horribly complex undertaking with lots of sacrifices and lots of interference from demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:10:47-08:00","id":72573,"title":"","content":"Mmm... not really. Because the God Machine can always end up saying, &quot;Angels are a priority right now, lets start mass production of new ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really think that the God Machine is going to be doomed since he can create new angels from a renewable resource (human sacrifices). Demons only renew their numbers by corrupting angels, which is risky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2014, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T08:30:25-08:00","id":72635,"title":"","content":"Also, I would like to point out, who says there aren't some very clever, well hidden, pieces of infrastructure somewhere whose only purpose is to produce new run-of-the-mill angels? Perhaps even spitting out one every few years.<br /> My own first thought on the matter is &quot;Those things they photographed on Mars, that looked like pyramids... coincidence?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}